moos-ivp (24.8.1+dfsg-4) trixie; urgency=high

  * Security fixes from upstream's main branch, as patches:
    - alogsplit: create the split directory without a shell, and reduce a
      log variable name to a safe file name (CVE-2026-85439, CVE-2026-85456).
    - iSay, uMemWatch: run commands without a shell (CVE-2026-85425,
      CVE-2026-85426).
    - uFldShoreBroker: refuse a ping whose keyword doesn't match, and bound
      how many nodes may enrol (CVE-2026-85434, CVE-2026-85448).
    - uFldNodeBroker: make runtime shore routes opt in (CVE-2026-85435).
    - uFldNodeComms: bind a node message to the community it came from, and
      bound how many nodes are tracked (CVE-2026-85429, CVE-2026-85446).
      Missions where pMarineViewer posts NODE_MESSAGEs for vehicles need
      BIND_MSG_SRC_TO_COMMUNITY = false.
    - IvP function decoders: bound the BHV_IPF copies and scans, validate the
      counts a payload declares, and bound the mux header (CVE-2026-85437,
      CVE-2026-85438, CVE-2026-85445).
    - isQuoted(), isBraced(), isChevroned(): index the stripped string with
      its own length (CVE-2026-85444).
    - Bound the .ipf file parser, free the StringToIvPContext buffer, and
      re-check for an empty string in setVarDataPairOnString().
  * pRealm: bound REALMCAST_REQ subscriptions, from upstream pull request
    #132, not yet merged (CVE-2026-85447).
  * pMarineViewer: bound how many distinct vehicles are tracked, with a new
    MAX_NODE_COUNT (default 200). Upstream has no fix yet (CVE-2026-85449).

 -- Toby Schneider <toby@gobysoft.org>  Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +1100

moos-ivp (24.8.1+dfsg-3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Stop shipping the IvP and MOOSGeodesy headers in libmoos10-mit-dev,
    and the MOOS core headers in libmoos-ivp-dev, so the two can be
    installed together. libmoos-ivp-dev now depends on libmoos10-mit-dev.

 -- Toby Schneider <toby@gobysoft.org>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +1000

moos-ivp (24.8.1+dfsg-2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Add SOVERSION to libMOOSGeodesy so dh_shlibdeps can generate an
    automatic Depends on libmoos-ivp for packages linking against it
    (e.g. moos-ivp-apps).
  * Install the new versioned libMOOSGeodesy.so.* into libmoos-ivp, and
    move the unversioned libMOOSGeodesy.so dev symlink to
    libmoos-ivp-dev, matching the libmoos10-mit/libmoos10-mit-dev split.

